Subject: [PATCH] GPU renderer: keyboard prompts, frame-mode pictures in
 full, points as dots

A texture pack's keyboard/ folder replaces textures while the keyboard
is the device in use (ps2_host_input::keyboardPromptsShown), switching
from one picture to the next.

An interlaced frame-mode display (224-row buffers for 448 lines) keeps
the buffers it shows at twice the scale down and shows each row as the
two lines it becomes, so the picture has every line of its own instead
of half as many (PS2X_GPU_FRAME_LINES=0: as before); textures drawn into
those buffers are smoothed.

Points added to the frame (Cs x C + Cd) are drawn as soft dots at their
exact place, their weights summing to one pixel's light, instead of a
block of the scale's size (PS2X_GPU_ROUND_POINTS=0: blocks).
